+## UBU-D0381: Multimodal qualification verifies backend release after cancellation
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §1. Narrows `UBU-Q0177`; measured hardware selection remains Open.
+
+Extend `UBU-D0331`/`UBU-D0336`'s cancellation and reuse evidence to actual backend quiescence, source-dependent buffer cleanup and runtime/worker resource release. Cancellation status, process exit or worker disconnection alone cannot establish complete-route release. Keep outstanding work generation-bound, prevent premature buffer reuse and withhold further dispatch through an affected runtime instance while release is unconfirmed. Immediate invalidation, controls and useful manual completion remain independent of backend progress.
+
+Charge unresolved resources and any qualified fallback to the same aggregate limits; neither containment nor pending cleanup extends existing release or retention deadlines. Require delayed-completion, repeated-cancellation, teardown-failure and late-callback/write fixtures with actual lifecycle observations, plus real-device evidence and costs in the existing support matrix. Disconnected workers require endpoint-local enforcement and truthful unconfirmed remote-release status.
+
+This specifies evidence for the existing bounded-release gate without supplying passing results, selecting hardware or changing the mobile planning/API allocation. `UBU-Q0177` remains Open pending the complete mandatory-slice evidence and operator approval.
